{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "02749",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 0.73,
      "end_seconds": 4.9,
      "duration_seconds": 4.17,
      "text": "Hi, sit anywhere you like. What's been worrying you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 6.45,
      "end_seconds": 8.96,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "It's fainting on exertion, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.04,
      "end_seconds": 14.22,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "What's the timeline, when did it begin?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 15.58,
      "end_seconds": 18.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "about... well, about a week"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 19.91,
      "end_seconds": 28.39,
      "duration_seconds": 8.48,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 29.55,
      "end_seconds": 66.97,
      "duration_seconds": 37.42,
      "text": "Yes, exertion. That makes it worse. It happens once or twice a day. Maybe a eight out of ten on a bad day. I took the morning off to come in today. As for swollen ankles, I honestly can't say when that began. It might have been last month or the month before. Uh, as for swollen ankles, I'd say once or twice a day. I did have chest tightness at one point, uh, but that's gone now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.82,
      "end_seconds": 74.14,
      "duration_seconds": 5.32,
      "text": "let me check a few things. Any leg pain, fever or cough?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 75.19,
      "end_seconds": 77.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "Nope, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.26,
      "end_seconds": 81.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 83.52,
      "end_seconds": 85.65,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 86.86,
      "end_seconds": 91.6,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Let's talk a little about your daily life and habits."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.2,
      "end_seconds": 103.32,
      "duration_seconds": 10.12,
      "text": "I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I live with my elderly mother. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 104.42,
      "end_seconds": 107.44,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Before we go further, any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.25,
      "end_seconds": 118.09,
      "duration_seconds": 8.84,
      "text": "uh, I was told I'm allergic to kiwi, but I don't remember what reaction I had"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.82,
      "end_seconds": 131.17,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "Are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.12,
      "end_seconds": 136.13,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "Allopurinol, 100 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 149.12,
      "end_seconds": 151.58,
      "duration_seconds": 2.46,
      "text": "Do you have any long-term conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 155.67,
      "end_seconds": 160.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "Okay, uh, so I've had gout for two years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 168.05,
      "end_seconds": 176.34,
      "duration_seconds": 8.29,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Pulse is 91 beats a minute, BP is 129 over 81, temperature is 36.8 degrees."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 177.23,
      "end_seconds": 177.93,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "thanks"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.43,
      "end_seconds": 182.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "let's move on to the examination"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.15,
      "end_seconds": 186.85,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Yes, um, that's fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 188.02,
      "end_seconds": 190.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Hold that that for a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 204.6,
      "end_seconds": 210.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.48,
      "text": "There is a loud second heart sound and a raised jugular pulse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.82,
      "end_seconds": 228.4,
      "duration_seconds": 15.58,
      "text": "good, you can sit up again. Let me tell you where I've got to. It points towards possible pulmonary hypertension. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.45,
      "end_seconds": 231.13,
      "duration_seconds": 1.68,
      "text": "Is this permanent?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.96,
      "end_seconds": 259.6,
      "duration_seconds": 26.64,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with possible pulmonary hypertension do well once it's treated properly. I'm sending you for an ECG because of syncope. The result will help us decide whether anything more is needed. Let's get an echocardiogram, for exertional syncope. No exertion for now, I am arranging urgent specialist tests. I think the pulmonary hypertension service should see you too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 261.07,
      "end_seconds": 264.64,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "Should I have blood tests as well?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 267.57,
      "end_seconds": 278.65,
      "duration_seconds": 11.08,
      "text": "not right now, it wouldn't change what we do today if the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please come to the emergency department"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 282.86,
      "end_seconds": 283.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.04,
      "text": "I understand"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.33,
      "end_seconds": 297.54,
      "duration_seconds": 12.21,
      "text": "Let's plan a check in one week. Can you tell me the plan back in your own words, so I know I've explained it clearly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 299.11,
      "end_seconds": 304.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "so, I come back in one week is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.21,
      "end_seconds": 313.05,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "Right, yes, exactly right. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.07,
      "end_seconds": 318.11,
      "duration_seconds": 3.04,
      "text": "Great, thank you for your help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.4,
      "end_seconds": 322.59,
      "duration_seconds": 1.19,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}